- Round 1: tests/v1/engine/test_request_submission_cleanup.py adds 6 tests (11 cases): text-only requests on a fast-path engine whose renderer must not be read, disconnect during materialization (n=1, 3), disconnect during a stripped send, failed submissions, the output handler starting on a fast-path engine (the boot failure), and abort during a cache-miss retry's materialization. test_prefix_cache_fastpath.py's lookup stub now returns get_computed_blocks' three values and checks them against KVCacheManager's annotation. On spark-ds41f:candidate-54 with candidate-55-r1's changed files mounted (sp8): test_request_submission_cleanup.py and test_api_cancellation.py 62 passed (candidate-55's files: the release's 13 failed, 38 passed); the PR's pytest command 45 passed on two boots; tests/v1/engine and tests/entrypoints/serve/utils 255 passed, 17 failed, 6 errors (candidate-55: 231 passed, 30 failed, the same 6 errors; the 17 and 6 are environmental and shared: async tests without an async plugin, hub models absent offline, no ray). A real AsyncLLM frontend with the recipe's multimodal flags constructs and serves a text request and a two-turn image chat (candidate-55: NameError in __init__).
- Round 2: tests/v1/core/test_stripped_mm_scheduling.py (new, 4 tests): a stripped item held nowhere is a retryable miss and its resubmission runs; one in the encoder cache is scheduled; a chunked prefill that reaches an evicted stripped item; a miss does not hold other requests. tests/v1/engine/test_request_submission_cleanup.py adds 6: every sampled child keeps its retry materializers, the retry runs off the output handler, a miss after returned output ends with an error, a stop-string finish drops the retry entry, bounded marks, streaming-input items keep their data. test_prefix_cache_fastpath.py adds the renderer's conditions, the real frontend built from the DS4.1 checkpoint sending repeated images without data only with --mm-processor-cache-gb 0, loading without the fast path as before, new items hashed alongside the HF processor equal to the plain path, the header digest alongside the decode and a pre-key collision. On spark-ds41f:candidate-54 with candidate-55-r2's changed files mounted (sp8): test_request_submission_cleanup.py and test_api_cancellation.py 68 passed (round 1's files with the new tests: the 6 new AsyncLLM tests fail); #978's pytest command with test_stripped_mm_scheduling.py 56 passed on two boots (round 1's files: 9 failed, 5 errors); tests/v1/engine and tests/entrypoints/serve/utils 261 passed, 17 failed, 6 errors (candidate-54: 244 passed, 17 failed, 6 errors, recorded in round 1; the 17 and 6 are environmental and shared); test_scheduler.py, test_async_scheduler.py, test_encoder_cache_manager.py, tests/multimodal/test_processing.py, test_registry.py, test_inputs.py, test_image.py and tests/renderers/test_warmup.py, test_multimodal_hashes.py 153 passed, 2 failed, 1 error (candidate-54: the same). Round 1's real-AsyncLLM serving bench against candidate-54, ABBA, two boots each: turn 2+ 4.2x to 9.5x faster, turn 1 2% to 15% faster, in all six image workloads; text-only requests within the interval.

